error[NK1201]: You can't put `Bytes` in an `f"…"` hole.
  --> tests/bytes_in_a_text_hole_is_refused.nika:5:5
   |
 5 |     let line = f"image {b}"
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: A hole is written as its value's text, and bytes are not text (ADR-019 D7). `b` is `Bytes`.
   = help: Print the bytes beside the line: `print(b)`, or write their text: `{b.text_lossy()}`.
error[NK1201]: You can't put `Bytes` in an `f"…"` hole.
  --> tests/bytes_in_a_text_hole_is_refused.nika:7:5
   |
 7 |     println(f"{Bytes([0x41])}")
   |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |
   = note: A hole is written as its value's text, and bytes are not text (ADR-019 D7). `Bytes([65])` is `Bytes`.
   = help: Print the bytes beside the line: `print(Bytes([65]))`, or write their text: `{(Bytes([65])).text_lossy()}`.
2 type errors
